 ## 2026-09-03
 
+### 0753 — Validate-then-alias is a bypass path, not a gate; and a clause claimed against the wrong actor
+
+- SCOPE: `internal/axerror` rework after review of CR-TASK-260830-34elja-1 rev1 returned `changes_requested` with two blocking findings, both reproduced by the reviewer.
+- ROOT CAUSE: **a validator that checks a graph the constructed value does not own has run and then let the checked data change.** `New` validated the caller's `Details` map and kept it through a *shallow* `cloneDetails`; `Detail` handed the live nested container straight back. Only the top-level map was isolated. Through the package's own exported accessor - no cooperation from the constructing call site needed - a validated failure could be made to emit `"password":"hunter2"`, 33,036 bytes against a declared 16 KiB bound, a value 7 containers deep against a declared bound of 4, and a Go `int` that `validateDetailValue` refuses outright. `axerror.Decode` then rejected the package's own `MarshalJSON` output.
+- FINDING: every §15.1 detail bound was defeated by this, and **no test covered post-construction mutation** - all 20 mutants and the whole positive/negative suite only ever validated maps nobody touched afterwards. The exported doc comment claimed "the closed Section 15.1 object is the only shape this type can produce", which this board treats as a contract; it was false and undisclosed. `internal/config` already returns an isolated resolved-root snapshot for exactly this reason, so the convention existed and was not followed.
+- FIX: deep copy on the way in (`cloneDetails` → `cloneDetailValue`) and on the way out (`Detail`). Five new mutants, three of them **narrowings** rather than deletions - copy shallow again, deep copy stopped at one level, deep copy applied to maps but not arrays - and the tests attack containers at three depths and on both sides of an array so a one-level copy fails them. `internal/axerror/ownership_test.go`.
+- ROOT CAUSE: **a clause was claimed against a topically related section instead of against the actor its MUST binds.** Ownership clause `15.1#6` at SPEC.md:11047 was discharged by `LocalFromUntrusted`. That line's only RFC 2119 sentence is "The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2" - it binds the **provider plugin**, a child process this repository does not build; its only binaries are `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. The host half of the same table row, which `LocalFromUntrusted` does implement, carries no RFC 2119 keyword at all, so it is not what the clause scanner measured.
+- FINDING: the scanner counts lines matching an RFC 2119 keyword; it cannot decide **which noun** the MUST governs. A human reading the subject of the sentence is the only check there is. This is the same ground on which `15.1#5` was correctly declared undischarged in the same registry - the honest refusal and the inflated claim shipped side by side.
+- FIX: `15.1#6` dropped, the §15.1 `gap` now names both undischarged clauses with their reasons, digest pin recomputed. §15.1 6/7 → **5/7**, repository `clauses_discharged` 10/394 → **9/394**. This supersedes the EVIDENCE line of the 0742 entry below. No gate outcome moves: §15.1 stays `partial` and assigned-scope admission still refuses it.
+- NOTE: the 0742 entry credits a leading-quote guard in `decodeExitStatus` as the fix for the `"9"` string-exit-status defect. It was not - the real fix was reading `exit_code` from `json.RawMessage`, and the guard was unkillable dead weight in front of `strconv.ParseInt`, which already refuses quoted bytes. Guard removed, the refusal table widened to `"9"`, `""`, `9.5`, `1e1`, `true`, `[]`, `{}`, `[9]`, and a mutant that strips quotes before parsing - the exact narrowing a `json.Number` field would reintroduce - now reddens.
+- NOTE: rev1's harness verified several deletion mutants by grepping for an **unrelated** string that was present either way, which cannot distinguish "mutation applied" from "perl no-op". `run_mutant` now takes `present|absent` and a deletion is verified by the absence of the exact text it deleted.
+- EVIDENCE: 26 mutants, each verified applied before measurement, 26 killed, 0 survivors, final restore re-verified uncached. `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 across 12 packages; `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt -l` clean; `tracecheck` exit 0 at 9/394.
+- STATUS: Ready for review. TASK-260830-34elja rework, leaf 1 of 3 on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2jylym`.
